::PC_U02_L01_GP_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L01_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.7
Question:
Convert 30 degrees to radians. Which setup shows the correct conversion process
{
~A. 30 degrees multiplied by 180/π#This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
~B. 30 degrees divided by 180π#This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~D. 30 degrees plus π/180#This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
=C. 30 degrees multiplied by π/180#Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.\}

